@startuml usecase-console
' Who uses the system, and for what.
'
' The console is the whole human interface. The scheduler and the maintainer
' do not use it: the scheduler runs the refresh and the maintainer works on
' the code.

!include _style.puml
left to right direction

actor "Candidate" as Person
actor "Scheduler" as Sched
actor "Maintainer" as Dev

rectangle "The console" {
  usecase "Upload a resume" as UC1
  usecase "Read the parsed profile" as UC2
  usecase "Search the stored corpus" as UC3
  usecase "Read a job and its score" as UC4
  usecase "Tailor a resume for a job" as UC5
  usecase "Prepare an application" as UC6
  usecase "Approve or reject" as UC7
  usecase "Track the applications" as UC8
  usecase "Run the refresh" as UC9
}

Person --> UC1
Person --> UC2
Person --> UC3
Person --> UC4
Person --> UC5
Person --> UC6
Person --> UC7
Person --> UC8

Sched --> UC9 : runs the refresh
Dev --> UC9 : runs it by hand

note bottom of UC7
  The console never submits on its own.
  A person approves, and the approval
  is recorded with an identity and a time.
end note

@enduml
